1
00:00:04,793 --> 00:00:07,085
Time to eat.

2
00:00:11,275 --> 00:00:12,600
Hey.

3
00:00:13,526 --> 00:00:15,172
Is that enough food?

4
00:00:15,172 --> 00:00:17,933
Yeah, it's enough.

5
00:00:19,969 --> 00:00:23,441
You always eat so much, Taguchi.

6
00:00:24,987 --> 00:00:27,947
But I've never had that
from the convenience store before.

7
00:00:27,947 --> 00:00:28,980
Seriously?

8
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:30,380
Yeah.

9
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:41,219
Here.

10
00:00:56,283 --> 00:00:57,514
Good, right?

11
00:00:57,514 --> 00:00:58,874
Yeah!

12
00:01:01,498 --> 00:01:02,645
- Mr. Inoue.
- Yes?

13
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:05,290
This is Mr. Taguchi,
the new engineer stationed here.

14
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:07,742
Nice to meet you.
I'm Inoue from Sales &amp; Planning.

15
00:01:07,742 --> 00:01:09,470
I'm Taguchi. Pleased to meet you.

16
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,085
Likewise.

17
00:01:11,085 --> 00:01:12,772
Ms. Ohata.

18
00:01:12,772 --> 00:01:16,071
This is Mr. Taguchi,
who'll be stationed here starting today.

19
00:01:16,071 --> 00:01:19,079
I'm Taguchi. Pleased to meet you.

20
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:22,276
I'm Ohata. Nice to meet you.

21
00:01:22,902 --> 00:01:24,918
Thank you.

22
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:26,245
Let's continue.

23
00:01:29,608 --> 00:01:31,186
Oh, Ms. Yamane.

24
00:01:31,186 --> 00:01:33,159
- Yes?
- Well...

25
00:01:34,779 --> 00:01:38,736
This usage application form...

26
00:01:38,736 --> 00:01:41,450
Where do I get one?

27
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:45,645
There's an application form for that,
so I'll send it to you later.

28
00:01:49,843 --> 00:01:51,796
Let's eat.

29
00:01:52,802 --> 00:01:55,645
You still eat so little.

30
00:01:55,645 --> 00:01:57,342
Yeah.

31
00:01:57,342 --> 00:02:00,755
You're eating a lot, as always, huh?

32
00:02:00,755 --> 00:02:02,102
Yeah.

33
00:02:09,248 --> 00:02:10,688
Want some?

34
00:02:14,156 --> 00:02:18,398
I'm an adult now, so I'll pass.

35
00:02:20,317 --> 00:02:22,532
Where should I put this?

36
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,127
What do you mean, an adult?

37
00:02:42,243 --> 00:02:45,167
It's nothing.

38
00:04:10,761 --> 00:04:15,008
Hey, you should stop doing
that kind of thing.

39
00:04:16,233 --> 00:04:18,311
What kind of thing?

40
00:04:19,454 --> 00:04:21,101
I mean...

41
00:04:24,609 --> 00:04:27,077
Never mind. It's nothing.

42
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,332
Should you really be here?

43
00:04:31,332 --> 00:04:34,124
I bet you can make friends easily.

44
00:04:41,323 --> 00:04:44,396
So is it better if I don't come?

45
00:04:47,873 --> 00:04:49,759
Do whatever you want.

46
00:04:50,876 --> 00:04:53,521
I feel at ease here.

47
00:05:03,237 --> 00:05:06,185
[Yamane]

48
00:05:07,324 --> 00:05:11,892
Taguchi?
The one with blond hair and piercings?

49
00:05:12,506 --> 00:05:13,926
Yeah.

50
00:05:14,779 --> 00:05:16,576
Is he still blond?

51
00:05:16,576 --> 00:05:19,755
No, his hair is black now.

52
00:05:19,755 --> 00:05:23,501
Didn't he have
a ton of piercings in both ears?

53
00:05:23,501 --> 00:05:25,159
You remember well.

54
00:05:25,159 --> 00:05:29,173
Because back then,
you talked about Taguchi every day.

55
00:05:30,447 --> 00:05:32,314
Did I?

56
00:05:35,737 --> 00:05:38,208
That's amazing.

57
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:41,105
A reunion after ten years...

58
00:05:42,713 --> 00:05:46,708
Since you got to meet again,
why not go out for a meal?

59
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:52,292
We had lunch together,
but that was at work.

60
00:05:53,625 --> 00:05:55,565
And besides...

61
00:05:58,487 --> 00:06:01,469
I feel restless around him.

62
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:06,999
Oh? Restless, huh?

63
00:06:17,672 --> 00:06:19,977
I finished the cooperation request form.

64
00:06:19,977 --> 00:06:23,090
Thanks. I'll check it later.

65
00:06:24,865 --> 00:06:27,236
Also, I'm sorry.

66
00:06:27,236 --> 00:06:28,742
For what?

67
00:06:28,742 --> 00:06:31,182
For taking so long.

68
00:06:35,738 --> 00:06:40,534
Are you a bit tired?

69
00:06:40,534 --> 00:06:42,233
Huh?

70
00:06:42,233 --> 00:06:44,729
You've been doing new tasks lately.

71
00:06:45,752 --> 00:06:48,338
Which meeting record do you mean?

72
00:06:48,338 --> 00:06:51,207
I believe it was from the interim report.

73
00:06:51,207 --> 00:06:53,010
Understood. I'll check.

74
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:54,597
Thank you.

75
00:07:03,292 --> 00:07:05,258
Ms. Yamane?

76
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:10,017
Thank you for your concern,
but I'll do my best.

77
00:07:16,050 --> 00:07:18,165
That's tough.

78
00:07:18,165 --> 00:07:19,737
Huh?

79
00:07:19,737 --> 00:07:24,803
I hope there's a high school
that accepts our request to do a field test.

80
00:07:25,798 --> 00:07:27,445
Yeah.

81
00:07:33,704 --> 00:07:37,997
[The Regsarkana Sovereignty]
And that's what happened in Chapter One.

82
00:07:37,997 --> 00:07:40,190
Oh?

83
00:07:48,461 --> 00:07:50,459
I pushed this book onto you,

84
00:07:50,459 --> 00:07:53,713
and you're gonna read it soon too.

85
00:07:53,713 --> 00:07:56,148
I'm sorry for the spoilers.

86
00:07:56,148 --> 00:07:57,583
I got a little carried away.

87
00:07:57,583 --> 00:07:59,923
No, it's fine.

88
00:07:59,923 --> 00:08:02,245
I don't usually read books anyway.

89
00:08:02,245 --> 00:08:06,239
It's easier to read
when you explain it like that.

90
00:08:12,352 --> 00:08:14,012
What happens next?

91
00:08:16,218 --> 00:08:20,206
In Chapter Two,
a character I really love shows up.

92
00:08:20,206 --> 00:08:23,181
He's a bit like you, Taguchi.

93
00:08:23,181 --> 00:08:28,162
Right, if I had to say
what I like about him exactly...

94
00:08:28,162 --> 00:08:30,270
That's a bit embarrassing, so don't tell me.

95
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:32,213
Huh?

96
00:08:32,213 --> 00:08:33,696
Why?

97
00:08:34,407 --> 00:08:36,155
"Why"?

98
00:08:40,747 --> 00:08:42,849
I should get going.

99
00:08:42,849 --> 00:08:44,189
Huh?

100
00:08:46,212 --> 00:08:47,692
To class.

101
00:08:51,096 --> 00:08:53,175
What is it?

102
00:08:53,175 --> 00:08:54,850
Well...

103
00:08:54,850 --> 00:09:00,499
It's just that... fun times really fly by.

104
00:09:00,499 --> 00:09:02,519
We have tomorrow anyway.

105
00:09:03,711 --> 00:09:08,257
Tomorrow,
I have an English vocab test fifth period,

106
00:09:08,257 --> 00:09:10,579
so I need to study at lunchtime.

107
00:09:22,495 --> 00:09:23,908
What?

108
00:09:25,957 --> 00:09:27,117
Ow...

109
00:09:29,049 --> 00:09:31,562
I might be here after school too.

110
00:09:32,366 --> 00:09:33,719
Oh...

111
00:09:35,887 --> 00:09:37,735
See you tomorrow.

112
00:09:40,115 --> 00:09:41,935
See you tomorrow!

113
00:09:55,776 --> 00:09:58,638
[Taguchi: Can I show you something
on a video call today?]

114
00:10:21,061 --> 00:10:23,977
This angle is a bit low.

115
00:10:35,527 --> 00:10:37,327
And then...

116
00:10:39,922 --> 00:10:41,955
Good, that works.

117
00:10:49,388 --> 00:10:51,527
Sorry to keep you waiting!

118
00:10:51,527 --> 00:10:53,542
<i>Wait, are you working?</i>

119
00:10:54,696 --> 00:10:56,240
Sorry.

120
00:11:00,916 --> 00:11:03,603
You wear glasses at home?

121
00:11:04,371 --> 00:11:07,142
Yeah, is it weird?

122
00:11:07,142 --> 00:11:10,985
<i>Oh, no, it just feels new to me.</i>

123
00:11:11,663 --> 00:11:14,831
<i>So, what was it you wanted to show me?</i>

124
00:11:14,831 --> 00:11:16,650
Oh, right.

125
00:11:17,515 --> 00:11:18,640
This.

126
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:22,150
[The Regsarkana Sovereignty]
Is that a new release?

127
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:23,851
Yeah.

128
00:11:23,851 --> 00:11:26,379
The same series you gave me.

129
00:11:27,043 --> 00:11:30,293
<i>But you said you don't read books.</i>

130
00:11:30,293 --> 00:11:33,582
You're the reason I started reading, Yamane.

131
00:11:33,582 --> 00:11:34,829
Huh?

132
00:11:37,396 --> 00:11:41,374
Right. You said a character you like
resembles me?

133
00:11:42,267 --> 00:11:44,807
Yeah, he's like you, Taguchi.

134
00:11:44,807 --> 00:11:46,789
Why do you like him?

135
00:11:49,555 --> 00:11:52,108
Well...

136
00:11:56,567 --> 00:12:00,439
I can't really put it into words.

137
00:12:01,866 --> 00:12:03,372
I see.

138
00:12:05,649 --> 00:12:09,649
How about lately?
Read any interesting novels?

139
00:12:10,825 --> 00:12:13,658
Lately? Let me think.

140
00:12:15,115 --> 00:12:16,197
Yeah, so then,

141
00:12:16,197 --> 00:12:22,419
<i>he wakes up in a lighthouse,
which is so interesting to me.</i>

142
00:12:24,902 --> 00:12:28,362
<i>I'm so sorry! I spoiled it again.</i>

143
00:12:28,362 --> 00:12:32,472
No, it's fun hearing your explanations.

144
00:12:32,472 --> 00:12:35,156
You're just a good listener, Taguchi.

145
00:12:35,156 --> 00:12:36,708
<i>I see.</i>

146
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,776
It's already so late.

147
00:12:42,776 --> 00:12:45,420
<i>Oh, you're right.</i>

148
00:12:47,579 --> 00:12:51,197
It's late today, so I should probably go.

149
00:12:51,197 --> 00:12:54,364
Oh, right! Sorry for keeping you up.

150
00:12:54,364 --> 00:12:55,377
Well then...

151
00:12:55,377 --> 00:12:58,771
<i>Wait, Yamane.</i>

152
00:12:58,771 --> 00:13:00,172
What?

153
00:13:01,408 --> 00:13:04,323
I couldn't say it yesterday or today, but...

154
00:13:06,901 --> 00:13:08,553
See you tomorrow.

155
00:13:14,344 --> 00:13:16,215
See you tomorrow.

156
00:13:33,577 --> 00:13:35,991
See you tomorrow.

157
00:13:50,753 --> 00:13:52,634
Good work.

158
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,534
Good work.

159
00:14:13,379 --> 00:14:15,619
Wanna get lunch together?

160
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,133
Sure.

161
00:14:30,431 --> 00:14:32,031
Seriously?

162
00:14:32,897 --> 00:14:34,864
What's wrong?

163
00:14:34,864 --> 00:14:36,726
Our parent company emailed us.

164
00:14:36,726 --> 00:14:40,192
They want a detailed offerings report
within the day.

165
00:14:40,192 --> 00:14:41,278
What?

166
00:14:41,278 --> 00:14:43,864
But they said that was next week.

167
00:14:43,864 --> 00:14:46,362
There isn't enough time today.

168
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:50,657
If it's tough, I can help.

169
00:14:50,657 --> 00:14:52,685
I can't let you do that.

170
00:14:54,669 --> 00:14:56,515
I'll help too.

171
00:14:56,515 --> 00:14:59,296
But what about your own work, Ms. Yamane?

172
00:14:59,296 --> 00:15:03,097
Mine can definitely wait till tomorrow.

173
00:15:03,097 --> 00:15:06,020
I don't know if I can be useful, but...

174
00:15:07,185 --> 00:15:09,473
You're right.

175
00:15:09,473 --> 00:15:12,080
Let's all do it together.

176
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:14,861
But first,
I'll go talk to the parent company people.

177
00:15:14,861 --> 00:15:16,001
Huh?

178
00:15:16,001 --> 00:15:20,738
We'll make a proper draft,
but I'll adjust their expectations.

179
00:15:20,738 --> 00:15:22,744
Thank you.

180
00:15:26,049 --> 00:15:28,565
Does she think I'm unreliable?

181
00:15:28,565 --> 00:15:30,319
Huh?

182
00:15:30,319 --> 00:15:33,254
I think she's just being considerate.

183
00:15:33,991 --> 00:15:36,067
I hope so.

184
00:15:37,092 --> 00:15:39,560
For now, I'll forward the email to you.

185
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:41,288
- Okay.
- Thank you.

186
00:15:41,288 --> 00:15:42,809
No problem.

187
00:15:50,869 --> 00:15:57,575
[Urgent work. Can't come. I'm really sorry.]

188
00:16:21,192 --> 00:16:31,613
[It's okay. Do your best!]

189
00:16:45,905 --> 00:16:48,365
[The Regsarkana Sovereignty]

190
00:16:57,626 --> 00:16:59,762
You seem happy today, Yamane.

191
00:16:59,762 --> 00:17:00,796
Huh?

192
00:17:00,796 --> 00:17:02,629
Did something good happen?

193
00:17:03,677 --> 00:17:07,716
Well, there's something
I'm kind of looking forward to after this.

194
00:17:07,716 --> 00:17:09,238
Is that so?

195
00:17:09,238 --> 00:17:14,290
Well, there's hardly any work left,
so you can go home for today.

196
00:17:15,131 --> 00:17:16,816
Thank you!

197
00:17:16,816 --> 00:17:19,344
Then I'll head out first.

198
00:17:23,104 --> 00:17:25,271
Good work.

199
00:17:26,296 --> 00:17:28,161
Huh?

200
00:17:28,161 --> 00:17:29,945
Is something wrong?

201
00:17:29,945 --> 00:17:33,971
The book title and barcode info don't match.

202
00:17:33,971 --> 00:17:36,419
Maybe they were stuck on the wrong data.

203
00:17:36,419 --> 00:17:41,388
A bunch of books came in at once
the other day.

204
00:17:42,018 --> 00:17:44,935
We'll need to redo them all.

205
00:17:49,166 --> 00:17:51,139
I'll do it.

206
00:17:51,139 --> 00:17:52,192
You will?

207
00:17:52,192 --> 00:17:55,182
I don't have practice today, so I'm free.

208
00:17:56,422 --> 00:17:58,848
Yamane, see you.

209
00:18:02,744 --> 00:18:04,411
See you tomorrow.

210
00:18:11,241 --> 00:18:12,656
Wait.

211
00:18:12,656 --> 00:18:15,049
[Send]

212
00:18:15,049 --> 00:18:16,449
[Sent]

213
00:18:18,044 --> 00:18:20,704
Done!

214
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:26,327
Thank you so much!

215
00:18:26,327 --> 00:18:28,548
It was nothing, really.

216
00:18:28,548 --> 00:18:30,019
No worries.

217
00:18:30,019 --> 00:18:31,798
It's late, so let's hurry home.

218
00:18:31,798 --> 00:18:33,824
- Okay.
- Got it.

219
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:40,255
By the way,
an approval email for the field test came in.

220
00:18:40,255 --> 00:18:41,744
Huh, already?

221
00:18:41,744 --> 00:18:44,888
Yes, isn't that great?

222
00:18:46,687 --> 00:18:51,105
The school that emailed us is this one.

223
00:18:51,105 --> 00:18:52,328
Huh?

224
00:18:53,316 --> 00:18:55,236
It's my Alma mater.

225
00:18:55,236 --> 00:18:56,583
What?

226
00:18:57,326 --> 00:19:01,136
I knew it was on our list, but...

227
00:19:01,136 --> 00:19:02,971
I see.

228
00:19:03,658 --> 00:19:06,541
I'd like to visit my own school too.

229
00:19:06,541 --> 00:19:08,487
Was your school around here?

230
00:19:08,487 --> 00:19:10,274
No, it's in Nagoya.

231
00:19:14,770 --> 00:19:18,334
Excuse me, I'll be heading out now.

232
00:19:19,839 --> 00:19:22,190
- Good work.
- Good work!

233
00:20:05,277 --> 00:20:07,038
Taguchi.

234
00:20:09,266 --> 00:20:11,053
Yamane?

235
00:20:12,307 --> 00:20:14,105
Thank goodness.

236
00:20:14,105 --> 00:20:15,798
You're still here.

237
00:20:19,024 --> 00:20:21,482
My meeting ran long too.

238
00:20:22,609 --> 00:20:24,509
I see.

239
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:30,831
What?

240
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:34,464
Did you want to see me that badly?

241
00:20:40,618 --> 00:20:42,025
Yeah.

242
00:20:48,736 --> 00:20:52,872
After you said, "see you tomorrow",

243
00:20:53,982 --> 00:20:56,349
I was just so anxious.

244
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:04,174
Not just today,

245
00:21:05,917 --> 00:21:07,570
but back then too.

246
00:21:10,509 --> 00:21:11,869
Huh?

247
00:21:18,562 --> 00:21:22,241
Being together is fun,

248
00:21:23,192 --> 00:21:27,561
and it's hard to wait till we meet again.

249
00:21:29,563 --> 00:21:32,026
Even when I was alone,

250
00:21:33,110 --> 00:21:36,586
I'd think about
the stuff that made me laugh

251
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:41,355
or what we'd talk about tomorrow.

252
00:21:41,355 --> 00:21:44,859
It was always on my mind.

253
00:21:51,428 --> 00:21:57,470
So being able to say
"see you tomorrow" to you again,

254
00:21:57,470 --> 00:22:00,387
like back then,

255
00:22:02,909 --> 00:22:05,296
makes me really happy.

256
00:22:10,690 --> 00:22:15,631
Sorry. What am I even saying?

257
00:22:17,797 --> 00:22:19,284
Bye, then.

258
00:22:29,434 --> 00:22:31,418
Today, I...

259
00:22:33,577 --> 00:22:35,462
I was anxious too.

260
00:22:37,416 --> 00:22:38,783
Huh?

261
00:22:43,879 --> 00:22:45,883
We only had a few months together...

262
00:22:48,583 --> 00:22:51,416
ten years ago,

263
00:22:56,297 --> 00:22:59,681
but I just couldn't forget about you, Yamane.

264
00:23:14,933 --> 00:23:16,534
I like you.

265
00:23:22,278 --> 00:23:24,439
I've always liked you.

266
00:23:34,166 --> 00:23:36,024
Will you...

267
00:23:37,641 --> 00:23:39,761
go out with me?

268
00:23:45,004 --> 00:23:46,643
If things go wrong,

269
00:23:46,643 --> 00:23:48,924
I feel like we can't even
go back to being friends.

270
00:23:48,924 --> 00:23:51,554
Let's ask Taguchi out on a date.

271
00:23:51,554 --> 00:23:54,814
If it's too much for you,
we can just stay friends like before.

272
00:23:54,814 --> 00:23:57,721
Is that really okay with you, Taguchi?

273
00:23:57,721 --> 00:23:59,934
I want to get closer to you.
